    explanation: "An explicit cleartextTrafficPermitted=true (or usesCleartextTraffic=true) exposes that host's data to interception and injection. Migrate it to HTTPS; if a legacy host is unavoidable, scope a single per-domain exception with pinning and a documented removal deadline instead of a blanket allow.",
